  "_README": "Permission rules for the Grace Hill competitive-intelligence work. Save this as ~/.claude/settings.json (on your Mac: /Users/<you>/.claude/settings.json). Today the only pre-approved tool is Skill, which is why every session asks 20-30 times.",
  "_HOW_IT_STAYS_SAFE": "DENY BEATS ALLOW, always, from any settings file. So the allow list opens whole connectors for reading, and the deny list below closes every tool that writes to a system of record, sends a message on your behalf, deletes, or pushes code. Those still stop and ask you every single time.",
